ex \"without written authorization from the pupil's parent or legal guardian\". On 2026-02-11 Nass voted Aye on Senate concurrence, which carried 18–15. That isn't near-unanimous, so the vote can carry the chair. `rests_on` lists the AB 103 vote page and bill text.\n- **Bills that don't carry the chair:** Nass cosponsored and voted for AB 963 (2022) and AB 510 (2023-24). Both are parental bills of rights with many unrelated parts, and each includes \"the right to determine the names and pronouns used for the child while at school.\" I coded them `multi-subject`, so they lean the same way but can't set the chair.\n- **Thinner points to check:**\n  - The AB 103 vote page prints the count as two separate pieces of text, so `tally_quote` holds only \"AYES - 18\". The 15 nays appear in the passage note.\n  - The prompt gives Nass's current term as \"unknown\". I coded every passage `in-term` because each Senate roll call lists him as voting.\n- **Left empty:** `needs_source` and `quotes`. None of the sources contain his own words, so there were no quotes to grade.\n\nA few connectors still need authorization in claude.ai connector settings: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey and WorkOS. The GitHub server also failed to connect. This task didn't need any of them.","ttft_ms":25308,"type":"result","duration_ms":50667,"uuid":"e4a5d522-8360-4d20-8472-95b5d0eb2225","ttft_stream_ms":1611,"time_to_request_ms":73,"first_content_frame_ms":1612,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
